# target.yaml
apiVersion: postgresql.cnpg.io/v1
kind: Cluster
metadata:
    name: pg
spec:
    instances: 1
---
# unmapped
coverage: mapped 1 of 3 user-set keys
unmapped:
    - path: auth.existingSecret
      kind: manual
      note: Create a CNPG basic-auth Secret; the Bitnami Secret layout differs.
    - path: auth.password
      kind: manual
      note: Create a CNPG basic-auth Secret; password values are never copied.
---
# checklist.md
# Migration checklist: pg

- [ ] Choose microservice import for one database (roles are not imported) or monolith import for several databases (roles lose SUPERUSER; postgres is skipped). ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/database_import))
- [ ] Stop writes on the source before the final import; later changes are not copied. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/database_import))
- [ ] Use a destination PostgreSQL major at least as new as the source; destination pg_dump is used. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/database_import))
- [ ] Size PGDATA for the staged dump, data, and indexes. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/database_import))
- [ ] Ensure the source is reachable and the import user can run pg_dump and read roles. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/database_import))
- [ ] CloudNativePG defaults ssl_min_protocol_version to TLSv1.3; verify whether clients need TLS 1.2. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/postgresql_conf))
- [ ] On PostgreSQL 14+, review any md5 pg_hba rules before the default scram-sha-256 catch-all. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/postgresql_conf))
- [ ] Resolve auth.existingSecret: Create a CNPG basic-auth Secret; the Bitnami Secret layout differs. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/cloudnative-pg.v1))
- [ ] Resolve auth.password: Create a CNPG basic-auth Secret; password values are never copied. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/devel/cloudnative-pg.v1))

